/// Costs table partition - Fabric SQL-endpoint connection swap (Decision 4).
///
/// This replaces ONLY the Costs partition source in the existing report's
/// Shared.Dataset/definition/tables/Costs.tmdl. Every column, hierarchy, measure,
/// relationship, and visual in the report is reused verbatim. The single change is
/// the data source: ftk_Storage(...) becomes ftk_FabricSql(...).
///
/// Because the Delta table is already FOCUS-normalized by the toolkit's KQL transform
/// (the single transform owner), the heavy client-side normalization the storage
/// variant applies to raw exports is not needed here - the SQL endpoint serves
/// FOCUS-shaped rows directly.
///
/// Mode is directQuery: immediate value, license-agnostic, layout-insensitive. The
/// DirectLake upgrade is authorized only by the readiness gate (04_directlake_readiness),
/// never assumed.

partition Costs-fabric-sql = m
	mode: directQuery
	queryGroup: Fabric
	source = ```
			let
			    // Connection swap: read FOCUS-shaped Costs from the Fabric SQL endpoint.
			    // Replaces: RawData = ftk_Storage("focuscost")
			    Costs = ftk_FabricSql("focuscost")
			in
			    Costs
			```
